{
  "_note": [
    "What a model IS, for the card that shows beside a model chip: who made it, in",
    "what year, whether its weights are open, and how big it is.",
    "",
    "Every entry is a factual claim and carries the page it was read off. A model",
    "this file says nothing about shows no card -- an unknown fact stays unstated,",
    "it is never filled in from memory.",
    "",
    "Keys are the BARE model name (the part after the last '/') for text models and",
    "the output config id for image models. Bare, because the same model reaches",
    "this installation through whichever provider is configured, and a key carrying",
    "one provider's prefix would go silent the moment the operator switches.",
    "",
    "openness: 'open' = weights and training data published; 'weights' = weights",
    "downloadable, use restricted by the licence; 'closed' = no weights.",
    "params_b counts BILLIONS, and for an image model it is the image network",
    "alone -- its text encoder is a separate, exchangeable model. The size class",
    "shown beside the size (micro / small / large / very large) is read off",
    "params_b at four bits per weight; the thresholds stand in one place,",
    "public/ai4artsed-frontend/src/composables/useModelRegister.ts (sizeClass).",
    "A closed model without a published count is very large;",
    "any other model without a published count has no class.",
    "medium: image marks an image network. The size class is read for",
    "language models only: its thresholds were set from language-model",
    "examples (small = up to 32 B); on an image network, where 8 B",
    "is the top of the field, they wrote small beside SD 3.5 Large.",
    "An image network carries its count alone; a closed one",
    "without a published count is still very large.",
    "",
    "name and country are what a list of language models shows a model as:",
    "'Qwen 3.8 (China 2026) 27b' (useModelRegister.modelLabel). name is the",
    "model's own name without its size, which follows it from params_b.",
    "country is the maker's, and 'makers' at the end records it with the page",
    "it was read off: the seat of the maker or of the group it belongs to",
    "(Google DeepMind: Google LLC), as an ISO 3166 code; a consortium across",
    "several European countries is '150', the UN code for Europe. The surface",
    "names it in the reader's language (Intl.DisplayNames), so no word for",
    "the reader stands here."
  ],

